{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:32Z","created_by_operation":"op_8f585a2d38c640e489adfb833b97c4be","id":"pg_0bcc10aff3db526ab46f50d422b3a77d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/2389-research-packnplay-docs-release-process-md-5abeea291783-50d422b3a77d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3210c9724055570381824fcb4ce06cd9"],"title":"2389-research/packnplay/docs/release-process.md @ 5abeea291783","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:32Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8f585a2d38c640e489adfb833b97c4be"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:32Z","created_by_operation":"op_8f585a2d38c640e489adfb833b97c4be","id":"pg_3444428a901a5099b849e90d6dca4531","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/2389-research-packnplay-docs-docker-autobuilds-md-5abeea291783-e90d6dca4531.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_dca7079f47ab58cebdb1807c6265835f"],"title":"2389-research/packnplay/docs/docker-autobuilds.md @ 5abeea291783","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:29:32Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8f585a2d38c640e489adfb833b97c4be"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1b411e740c29587653e1e47ee10b3e51e0e99040316f3c5d30859ec9660d64ab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned CLI exposes four subcommands: run (with path, worktree, no-worktree, env, and verbose flags), attach, stop, and list, with attach and stop accepting path and worktree flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1e888e5793ef069fda7d80fb09a9115ea1e56cf9bbbabaeb6b9f33568759e1cd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plan specifies parsing .devcontainer/devcontainer.json for image, dockerFile, and remoteUser fields, defaulting remoteUser to devuser, and falling back to a default Ubuntu devcontainers image config when no devcontainer file exists."},{"claim_ids":["clm_32d9e93b0cb1707578304da17f73f3c3439a4ac2a56abfbab4e50eb0b7775069"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the plan follows a test-first workflow per task — write a failing test, implement, re-run go test to verify it passes, then commit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ede4bc1da0046ce8e99979790b54a298b2c7298ee0dea1c49bd7a43c53a6b86"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the plan document instructs the implementing agent to use the superpowers:executing-plans sub-skill to implement the plan task-by-task."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4bc7d8cde20e3290a1bae1b3b4be8cd1f14801b1e94a519b2d6249951337b17f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned tech stack is Go 1.21+, the cobra CLI framework, and the Docker and git CLIs invoked via shell."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4f97b53d2f51f977de26991a9e1bc359183a0869db572842761dce2a52f43945"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The evidence consists only of an implementation plan; the run, attach, stop, and list commands are specified with TODO placeholders, so actual implemented behavior at this commit is not evidenced by these slices."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5319cd5775e33e39f41437c598d82fc38335d7ba72994d4ea51d9840bebbe807"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plan's stated goal is to build packnplay, a CLI tool that launches commands such as Claude Code inside isolated Docker containers with automated worktree and dev container management."},{"claim_ids":["clm_534b4ba5084422dd71da7164911d0f4e89e7fb2b272d206ce841a1085c41ee3e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned architecture is a single Go binary using cobra for the CLI that shells out to docker and git commands, uses idmap mounts for UID translation, and tracks container state via session-based Docker labels."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a0b821f97eb2361c55a28964cdd1a8d1d690e0168a0111412ef0a6bf76cb590b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Planned worktree paths are computed as a sibling directory of the project named <project>-<sanitized-branch>, with branch names sanitized for filesystem safety."},{"claim_ids":["clm_efe5496ea728902481eab0ce66c642cb95f0e06c1145cc88c98a57cc71095a9a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Planned container naming combines a packnplay prefix, project name, and sanitized worktree name (slashes, spaces, and colons replaced with dashes), and containers carry managed-by, packnplay-project, and packnplay-worktree labels."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f61b1def94c89f3ec072ba41225a556370a610a6fe0f357656368ff227d9e2eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned Docker client detects the container CLI by honoring a DOCKER_CMD environment variable override, then falling back to docker and then podman in PATH."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1b411e740c29587653e1e47ee10b3e51e0e99040316f3c5d30859ec9660d64ab","clm_1e888e5793ef069fda7d80fb09a9115ea1e56cf9bbbabaeb6b9f33568759e1cd","clm_32d9e93b0cb1707578304da17f73f3c3439a4ac2a56abfbab4e50eb0b7775069","clm_3ede4bc1da0046ce8e99979790b54a298b2c7298ee0dea1c49bd7a43c53a6b86","clm_4bc7d8cde20e3290a1bae1b3b4be8cd1f14801b1e94a519b2d6249951337b17f","clm_4f97b53d2f51f977de26991a9e1bc359183a0869db572842761dce2a52f43945","clm_5319cd5775e33e39f41437c598d82fc38335d7ba72994d4ea51d9840bebbe807","clm_534b4ba5084422dd71da7164911d0f4e89e7fb2b272d206ce841a1085c41ee3e","clm_a0b821f97eb236